WEBVTT

00:06.276 --> 00:08.069
[reporter 1] ...four-term
incumbent Gotham mayor

00:08.069 --> 00:11.698
Don Mitchell, Jr., was
found murdered last night in...

00:11.823 --> 00:13.450
[reporter 2]
...tough war on drugs...

00:13.450 --> 00:15.076
[reporters overlapping]

00:15.076 --> 00:16.453
...notorious Mafia
crime figure,

00:16.453 --> 00:17.495
Salvatore Maroni...

00:17.495 --> 00:18.872
[reporter 3] ...sources tell GC1

00:18.997 --> 00:21.124
that a warrant
for Falcone's arrest

00:21.124 --> 00:22.917
is suspected to reach...

00:22.917 --> 00:25.003
[reporter 4] ...the second
high-profile murder

00:25.128 --> 00:26.504
in as many nights.

00:26.629 --> 00:28.506
This time, the killer
hasn't come forward to claim...

00:29.382 --> 00:30.925
We interrupt
election coverage now

00:30.925 --> 00:32.093
for some breaking news.

00:32.093 --> 00:34.137
We are getting
unconfirmed reports

00:34.137 --> 00:38.224
about a series of explosions
along the city's seawall.

00:39.142 --> 00:42.437
[reporter 5] And we are live
watching the Batman vigilante

00:42.437 --> 00:44.147
atop Gotham Square Garden

00:44.272 --> 00:46.941
helping save the lives
of hundreds of injured victims

00:46.941 --> 00:49.778
after devastating explosions
took out the city's seawall.

00:49.778 --> 00:51.237
We will rebuild.

00:52.322 --> 00:53.615
But not just our city.

00:53.865 --> 00:57.160
Together, we will learn
to believe in Gotham again.

00:57.160 --> 00:58.328
It's been a week

00:58.495 --> 01:00.205
since the terrorist
known as The Riddler

01:00.330 --> 01:01.873
blew up Gotham's seawall.

01:01.873 --> 01:03.416
And as the death toll climbs,

01:03.583 --> 01:05.794
Gotham residents are demanding
answers from authorities.

01:05.794 --> 01:08.129
While the wealthier suburbs
have been spared,

01:08.129 --> 01:10.173
it's Gotham's
poorest neighborhoods

01:10.173 --> 01:12.967
that have been hit the hardest,
especially in Crown Point.

01:12.967 --> 01:15.136
[reporter 5] Looting and rioting
have become the norm.

01:15.136 --> 01:17.806
Combined with the scarcity
of illicit drugs

01:17.806 --> 01:19.391
and an increase
in gang warfare,

01:19.516 --> 01:21.768
the city has reached
a boiling point.

01:21.768 --> 01:24.688
The murder of longtime mob boss
Carmine Falcone

01:24.688 --> 01:26.314
outside the Iceberg Lounge

01:26.314 --> 01:28.983
has complicated efforts
to restore order,

01:28.983 --> 01:32.112
creating a power vacuum
in Gotham's underworld.

01:32.737 --> 01:33.988
[reporter 5] Rumors are swirling

01:33.988 --> 01:36.241
that Carmine's son,
Alberto Falcone,

01:36.449 --> 01:38.243
is set
to take his father's place

01:38.243 --> 01:40.578
despite his public struggles
with alcohol.

01:41.037 --> 01:42.747
[reporter 6] After this shakeup
in leadership,

01:42.747 --> 01:44.833
insiders worry
about their future

01:44.833 --> 01:48.420
within the Falcone organization
and wonder what will become

01:48.420 --> 01:51.089
of Gotham's
most notorious family.

01:51.089 --> 01:52.298
[dramatic music crescendos]

01:53.675 --> 01:55.969
- [sirens in distance]
- [train trundling]

01:56.094 --> 01:58.138
[somber music playing]

02:16.489 --> 02:17.282
[engine turns off]

02:17.407 --> 02:18.491
[rain pattering]

02:30.754 --> 02:33.840
[tense music playing]

02:57.530 --> 02:58.490
[elevator dings]

03:08.124 --> 03:12.796
[sirens in distance]

03:16.257 --> 03:18.093
[thunder rumbles]

03:28.186 --> 03:29.104
[thudding]

03:40.407 --> 03:41.825
[scraping]

03:56.172 --> 03:57.257
[Oz grunts]

04:07.892 --> 04:08.768
[chuckles]

04:09.853 --> 04:13.023
Oh, beautiful.
Beautiful, beautiful, beautiful.

04:14.816 --> 04:15.734
[pictures thump]

04:25.368 --> 04:26.286
[jewelry jangles]

04:27.370 --> 04:28.246
[gun cocks]

04:28.455 --> 04:30.206
I see you've made yourself
at home.

04:30.206 --> 04:32.042
[thunder rumbles]

04:32.709 --> 04:35.462
Hey, Alberto, you're here.

04:36.212 --> 04:38.423
Good. Saves me a trip.

04:38.548 --> 04:40.091
What the fuck
are you talking about?

04:40.216 --> 04:42.635
These jewels belong to you.

04:43.219 --> 04:44.512
Your dad made that clear.

04:45.096 --> 04:46.264
But some of the guys,

04:46.389 --> 04:48.558
well, you know,
they're goddamn scavengers.

04:48.558 --> 04:50.477
So I thought I'd do you a solid.

04:50.477 --> 04:52.020
As a show of support for...

04:53.313 --> 04:54.397
your new position.

04:55.690 --> 04:56.566
Well...

04:57.233 --> 04:58.443
congratulations.

04:59.736 --> 05:02.113
I only wish it had been
under different circumstances.

05:02.906 --> 05:03.782
Carmine...

05:05.158 --> 05:06.117
he was a...

05:07.327 --> 05:08.578
He was a great man.

05:09.537 --> 05:11.247
You got some big shoes to fill.

05:12.207 --> 05:13.917
[Oz chuckles]

05:13.917 --> 05:16.002
N-not too big.

05:16.127 --> 05:18.380
I mean, you know,
m-manageable shoes.

05:18.380 --> 05:20.215
You think I'm an idiot?

05:20.757 --> 05:22.092
You greedy prick.

05:22.092 --> 05:23.593
My father's been dead a week.

05:23.593 --> 05:25.053
Hey, Al.

05:26.805 --> 05:28.306
[sighs] You all right?

05:29.432 --> 05:32.143
'Cause we keep a stash
in the loft if you want a hit.

05:33.937 --> 05:35.063
That's not why I'm here.

05:35.063 --> 05:36.606
Of course not.
I was only saying--

05:36.606 --> 05:37.732
You don't get it.

05:37.732 --> 05:39.234
Everyone's looking to me now.

05:39.776 --> 05:43.238
I got this deal going, and...
[inhales sharply]

05:44.406 --> 05:46.408
I can't. I gotta
keep my head on straight.

05:46.408 --> 05:47.826
Yeah, you're right, Boss.

05:47.826 --> 05:49.828
I got no idea
the pressure you're under.

05:51.663 --> 05:54.499
But you're
Alberto Friggin' Falcone.

05:55.500 --> 05:57.544
The new kingpin of Gotham.

05:59.504 --> 06:01.631
[chuckles softly]
We should celebrate that.

06:03.299 --> 06:07.178
Listen, staying off the Drops,
good on you.

06:08.430 --> 06:09.848
But booze don't count.

06:10.348 --> 06:11.224
Does it?

06:12.517 --> 06:16.062
- [Oz and Alberto laughing]
- [jazz music playing]

06:18.857 --> 06:20.400
So this new deal
you got going...

06:21.109 --> 06:22.444
Maybe I can help.

06:22.444 --> 06:24.612
You know what
I like most about you, Oz?

06:25.155 --> 06:27.157
You are who you are.

06:27.157 --> 06:28.867
You couldn't change
if you tried.

06:28.867 --> 06:30.952
Ain't that what makes me fun?

06:30.952 --> 06:32.704
[laughing]

06:35.582 --> 06:36.666
Oh!

06:36.666 --> 06:38.293
Yeah, go on.

06:38.293 --> 06:39.878
[chuckling] Oh!
This shit's good.

06:40.003 --> 06:41.379
- Good.
- [Alberto sniffs]

06:41.379 --> 06:44.716
But after a while,
you get curious.

06:44.841 --> 06:46.760
There's gotta be something else
out there,

06:47.510 --> 06:49.054
a new kind of high.

06:49.929 --> 06:51.181
So you're gonna, what?

06:52.015 --> 06:53.224
Alter the formula?

06:53.349 --> 06:55.852
We're not just adding ketchup
to fries, man.

06:55.852 --> 06:59.314
I'm talking about
revolutionizing the game.

06:59.981 --> 07:02.233
Fuck. [chuckles]
Look at you salivating.

07:02.359 --> 07:04.277
[inhales] Fine.

07:06.571 --> 07:07.697
You got a girl?

07:08.323 --> 07:09.866
Good-looking guy like you...

07:11.326 --> 07:12.369
Here.

07:13.370 --> 07:14.788
Just keep quiet.

07:14.954 --> 07:17.415
I can't have Viti and those guys
knowing what I've got going

07:17.415 --> 07:19.542
until this new drug's
up on its feet.

07:21.544 --> 07:23.088
Thanks, Boss. It's, uh...

07:24.798 --> 07:26.091
real generous.

07:26.091 --> 07:28.176
Pop always said
you were a good soldier.

07:28.676 --> 07:30.345
It's what he liked most
about you.

07:32.138 --> 07:34.099
But he also knew
you were a dirty soldier

07:34.224 --> 07:35.975
who skims money off the top.

07:36.976 --> 07:39.229
It's okay, man.
You were smart about it.

07:39.229 --> 07:41.147
Never took enough
for Pop to mind.

07:41.773 --> 07:42.899
See, he knew what it meant

07:42.899 --> 07:44.943
for a guy like you
to get a piece.

07:46.236 --> 07:47.487
How it made you feel.

07:48.321 --> 07:50.073
And that was good for business.

07:50.657 --> 07:54.244
Carmine Falcone was a master
at the carrot and stick.

07:57.497 --> 07:58.623
See what I got on?

07:59.791 --> 08:01.960
Your dad's ring. Nice.

08:02.085 --> 08:03.420
Wasn't always his.

08:04.421 --> 08:05.922
Used to be Salvatore's.

08:07.132 --> 08:09.801
- Salvatore Maroni?
- He wore Sal's ring as a trophy.

08:09.926 --> 08:11.553
The ultimate fuck-you.

08:12.470 --> 08:15.098
This is power, right?

08:17.392 --> 08:18.268
Wanna try it on?

08:19.060 --> 08:19.936
Nah.

08:20.395 --> 08:21.271
It's yours.

08:22.647 --> 08:23.523
Yeah.

08:27.444 --> 08:29.279
I don't know, man. [sighs]

08:30.447 --> 08:32.407
You think I could be
as good as him?

08:32.991 --> 08:34.534
Get his kind of respect?

08:36.369 --> 08:37.245
Your father?

08:39.956 --> 08:40.999
Sure, Boss.

08:42.125 --> 08:43.001
If you want.

08:43.626 --> 08:45.503
But there are different kinds
of power.

08:48.465 --> 08:49.382
When I was kid,

08:50.425 --> 08:51.509
there was a gangster,

08:52.302 --> 08:53.762
real old-school type,

08:54.763 --> 08:55.930
Rex Calabrese.

08:56.890 --> 08:57.891
He was a big deal.

08:58.391 --> 09:00.185
Yeah. At least,
in my neighborhood.

09:01.478 --> 09:02.604
He helped people.

09:03.855 --> 09:05.607
When someone in your family
was sick,

09:06.107 --> 09:07.609
he'd find you a doctor.

09:08.943 --> 09:11.696
Short on rent,
front you the cash.

09:13.323 --> 09:14.824
Knew everyone's names, too.

09:16.826 --> 09:19.120
I don't know how he kept them
all in his head, but...

09:19.704 --> 09:20.997
He saw you on the street,

09:22.040 --> 09:23.083
he'd call out to you,

09:23.833 --> 09:24.709
ask how you were.

09:26.419 --> 09:27.712
Felt like he meant it, too.

09:29.047 --> 09:29.923
[chuckles softly]

09:31.383 --> 09:32.967
When I'm 14 or something,

09:33.802 --> 09:35.303
he has a heart attack and dies,

09:36.554 --> 09:38.014
still holding his cigar.

09:39.474 --> 09:40.600
In my neighborhood,

09:41.518 --> 09:43.228
they throw a parade
in his honor.

09:44.688 --> 09:46.064
A friggin' parade.

09:47.774 --> 09:49.984
I mean, it wasn't fancy,
but it was the gesture...

09:50.860 --> 09:51.820
the show of love...

09:52.862 --> 09:53.947
of what he meant.

09:55.407 --> 09:56.491
Can you imagine?

09:57.409 --> 09:59.077
To be remembered like that?

09:59.202 --> 10:00.370
Revered?

10:02.122 --> 10:03.039
What is this?

10:06.376 --> 10:09.921
You want me to be like
some small-time asshole?

10:12.257 --> 10:14.008
- Nah, that ain't--
- For what?

10:16.469 --> 10:18.972
Would that make it easier
for you to take what's mine?

10:22.559 --> 10:24.269
Or is this you?

10:25.311 --> 10:26.563
What you want?

10:26.563 --> 10:28.398
[somber music playing]

10:28.398 --> 10:29.399
No.

10:30.483 --> 10:34.612
[laughing]

10:34.612 --> 10:36.239
Holy shit, it is!

10:38.950 --> 10:40.243
This is your dream.

10:40.994 --> 10:42.662
[laughs] It's so sweet, too.

10:43.413 --> 10:44.664
And so pathetic.

10:45.373 --> 10:48.793
You really think people'd make
a float of your dumb face

10:48.918 --> 10:51.963
and march it down the street,
chanting your goddamn name?

10:52.088 --> 10:53.965
[laughs]

10:53.965 --> 10:56.301
"Oh, oh! Oswald Cobb.

10:56.426 --> 10:59.137
Remember him? What a guy!"

10:59.137 --> 11:00.972
[laughs]

11:00.972 --> 11:02.849
What a little bitch! [laughs]

11:03.641 --> 11:04.934
[gun firing]

11:07.854 --> 11:10.523
- [menacing music playing]
- [breathing heavily]

11:12.192 --> 11:13.276
[laughs]

11:31.544 --> 11:34.339
Aw, fu--

11:34.339 --> 11:37.092
[dramatic music playing]

11:37.092 --> 11:38.510
[body bag zipping]

11:52.023 --> 11:53.024
[phone clicks, beeps]

11:55.360 --> 11:56.569
[Oz grunts]

12:02.033 --> 12:03.868
[grunting]

12:09.332 --> 12:10.750
[tense music playing]

12:21.970 --> 12:24.973
- [grunts]
- [thudding]

12:25.724 --> 12:27.517
[tense music continues]

12:35.233 --> 12:36.234
[boy 1] Hurry up, bro.

12:36.359 --> 12:37.444
[boy 2] Relax. I got it.

12:37.902 --> 12:38.945
[boy 3] Hey, help him out.

12:39.279 --> 12:40.405
[boy 1]
Just turn the damn thing.

12:40.530 --> 12:41.865
Hey!

12:43.033 --> 12:43.908
Hey!

12:44.200 --> 12:45.535
- Oh, shi--
- [Oz] You sons of bitches!

12:45.535 --> 12:46.828
- [gun firing]
- [boy] Go! Go!

12:47.120 --> 12:48.496
Get the fuck out of here! Go!

12:48.496 --> 12:50.707
- [boy 1] Oh, shit!
- [boy 2] Hey!

12:50.832 --> 12:52.876
- Wait. Wait. Okay, I'm done.
- [boy 1] Go! Go!

12:53.001 --> 12:55.420
- Please! Please! All right.
- Don't you try and run.

12:55.420 --> 12:58.089
I'm sorry. I-I'm sorry.
I'm-- [grunts]

12:58.089 --> 13:00.008
Don't move,
you twat-faced little prick.

13:00.008 --> 13:01.342
Trying to steal my shit!

13:01.342 --> 13:02.260
[clanging]

13:02.385 --> 13:04.012
- Hey!
- Shut the fuck up.

13:04.554 --> 13:07.390
You wanna shout again?
You wanna fucking shout again?

13:07.390 --> 13:08.933
You messed with
the wrong fucking guy

13:08.933 --> 13:10.101
on the wrong fucking night.

13:10.101 --> 13:13.605
[spluttering] P-p-p...

13:13.605 --> 13:15.482
Please, please, please.

13:15.482 --> 13:17.525
- [whimpering]
- [tense music playing]

13:17.525 --> 13:19.110
Don't, okay, please?

13:19.235 --> 13:20.362
[mouthing soundlessly]

13:21.946 --> 13:24.199
P-please!

13:24.199 --> 13:26.451
- Please, don't--
- Jesus! Take a breath.

13:27.243 --> 13:28.078
What have we got here?

13:28.078 --> 13:29.746
[boy whimpers]

13:32.791 --> 13:34.959
"Victor Aguilar."

13:41.674 --> 13:43.259
I'm keeping your ID.

13:44.844 --> 13:46.012
Walk. That way.

13:47.722 --> 13:48.973
[tense music continues]

13:48.973 --> 13:50.100
[Victor grunts]

13:53.520 --> 13:54.312
Head first.

13:54.437 --> 13:57.607
[Victor grunting]

13:57.607 --> 13:59.734
Fucking foot! God damn it!

14:00.944 --> 14:02.987
[breathing heavily]

14:06.491 --> 14:08.159
- Hey! Hey, look at me.
- [gasps]

14:08.284 --> 14:09.577
How far do you think you'd get?

14:10.036 --> 14:12.831
This scumbag,
he disrespected me.

14:12.956 --> 14:14.666
- You gonna disrespect me, Vic?
- No. No.

14:14.666 --> 14:17.502
No. 'Cause you and me,
we're in this together now.

14:18.878 --> 14:20.505
Which means... [chuckles]

14:20.630 --> 14:21.756
I own you.

14:22.382 --> 14:23.299
[thud]

14:24.801 --> 14:26.469
Look what you
fucking made me do.

14:28.471 --> 14:30.014
You're gonna do
everything I say.

14:31.057 --> 14:33.184
Or else I'll murder you
and, uh...

14:33.184 --> 14:34.686
anyone you care about.

14:34.686 --> 14:36.813
- You got it?
- [weakly] Yeah.

14:37.856 --> 14:38.982
Beautiful.

14:39.107 --> 14:41.234
I feel better. You feel better?

14:42.235 --> 14:43.028
[weakly] Yeah.

14:43.153 --> 14:44.195
Good.

14:44.320 --> 14:45.947
Now, you wanted my car so badly,

14:46.406 --> 14:47.949
you can drive. [sniffs]

14:51.870 --> 14:52.746
Go on.

14:56.916 --> 14:58.209
[tense music continues]

15:16.811 --> 15:17.937
Make a left up here.

15:18.938 --> 15:20.190
Okay.

15:31.576 --> 15:32.994
[Oz] This fucking douchebag...

15:33.536 --> 15:34.412
[scoffs]

15:34.954 --> 15:36.289
Here we go.

15:41.628 --> 15:43.588
- Got you now, you piece of shit.
- [camera clicks]

15:44.881 --> 15:46.383
Uh, s-should I--

15:53.890 --> 15:54.933
[phone shatters]

15:56.226 --> 15:57.769
[exhales heavily]

16:02.232 --> 16:03.525
What do you think of this?

16:04.442 --> 16:06.695
It's a... little air freshener.

16:09.239 --> 16:10.865
Aqua Paradise.

16:12.325 --> 16:13.743
- You smell it?
- Mm-hmm.

16:13.743 --> 16:14.786
It's nice, huh?

16:18.123 --> 16:19.666
- It's nice, yeah.
- Mm-hmm.

16:20.458 --> 16:21.418
Yeah, it's nice.

16:23.211 --> 16:26.589
[clears throat]
194 Tower Avenue.

16:28.091 --> 16:29.634
The old tenement on Sixth.

16:31.177 --> 16:32.470
I'm from the Eastside, too.

16:33.012 --> 16:34.139
I mean, not Crown Point.

16:34.931 --> 16:36.266
Further out from the port.

16:39.561 --> 16:41.229
You ever been
to that corner mart?

16:42.480 --> 16:44.107
Uh, next to the...

16:44.649 --> 16:45.775
uh, Coin-O-Matic?

16:46.401 --> 16:47.736
Um...

16:49.696 --> 16:50.613
Buddy's?

16:50.613 --> 16:51.865
[laughing]

16:52.699 --> 16:53.867
Yeah, Buddy's.

16:53.992 --> 16:54.909
Oh, man.

16:55.952 --> 16:57.912
They still sell
those Slush Puppies?

16:58.788 --> 17:00.999
I th-think so.

17:01.666 --> 17:02.792
Me and my brothers,

17:03.543 --> 17:05.628
we used to go there
every day in the summer.

17:05.628 --> 17:08.006
You know, we'd mix the flavors
for a suicide.

17:09.090 --> 17:10.300
You ever mix the flavors?

17:10.300 --> 17:11.259
Huh-uh.

17:12.218 --> 17:13.511
Aw. You missed out.

17:16.431 --> 17:18.641
You know, but I'd like to.

17:19.350 --> 17:21.728
You know, like in the...
in the future.

17:23.730 --> 17:24.773
Take a left here.

17:25.482 --> 17:26.608
[tense music continues]

17:33.531 --> 17:35.533
[dance music playing inside]

17:35.533 --> 17:38.036
[woman] Hi, Daddy.
Wanna come party with us?

17:38.036 --> 17:40.205
[woman 2] Nice car.
Can I get a ride?

17:41.956 --> 17:45.335
Wh-wh-what about the body?
Is that safe on the street?

17:45.335 --> 17:46.878
Why?
Your friends wanna steal it?

17:48.129 --> 17:50.006
Do me a favor, kid.
Shut your goddamn mouth.

17:50.006 --> 17:53.009
- Lookin' good. Ladies.
- [women] Hey, Oz.

17:53.009 --> 17:54.302
- Who is this?
- Good to see you.

17:54.302 --> 17:55.553
Looks brand-new.

17:55.553 --> 17:56.971
Like what you see, sweetie?

17:56.971 --> 17:58.264
[women laugh]

18:00.934 --> 18:02.060
[door closes]

18:03.061 --> 18:04.979
[indistinct chatter in distance]

18:07.023 --> 18:09.818
[metal clanking]

18:15.824 --> 18:16.700
[doorbell rings]

18:21.246 --> 18:22.414
- [Oz] Hey.
- Oz.

18:23.289 --> 18:24.165
Baby.

18:24.749 --> 18:26.710
- Everything okay?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

18:26.710 --> 18:28.128
Who's your friend?

18:29.713 --> 18:30.797
Eh...

18:31.339 --> 18:32.549
You alone?

18:33.258 --> 18:36.678
I, uh... I ain't trying
to get in your business, but...

18:37.929 --> 18:39.347
I need an alibi.

18:40.390 --> 18:41.808
Ideally, for the whole night.

18:42.851 --> 18:44.102
Sounds like we had fun.

18:44.644 --> 18:47.022
I'm serious, Eve. Yeah.

18:47.564 --> 18:48.606
Can you help me out?

18:49.107 --> 18:51.026
Anytime after 10,
but not before.

18:51.026 --> 18:52.902
All right, that'll work.

18:55.655 --> 18:57.032
- Thanks, doll.
- [bills rustling]

18:57.032 --> 18:58.575
I'll, uh, call ya.

19:05.915 --> 19:07.417
You hungry?
I'm hungry. Let's go.

19:12.464 --> 19:13.465
[Oz] Stupid night.

19:21.848 --> 19:23.933
I asked for extra pickles,
and they give me two?

19:24.642 --> 19:26.644
So what, a normal amount
of pickles is one?

19:27.187 --> 19:28.688
Makes no goddamn sense.

19:33.860 --> 19:35.028
You want one of mine?

19:35.695 --> 19:37.072
Do I want one of your pickles?

19:37.364 --> 19:38.782
That your dirty little mouth
touched?

19:38.782 --> 19:39.824
No, kid, I don't.

19:39.949 --> 19:41.701
[chuckling incredulously] Jesus.

19:43.870 --> 19:45.622
Shit! Would you look at that?

19:47.332 --> 19:49.084
Imagine if you
and your buddies came here

19:49.084 --> 19:50.585
instead of trying
to steal from me.

19:52.754 --> 19:54.422
Coulda saved you
a lot of trouble.

19:54.422 --> 19:56.049
What was your plan anyway?

19:56.174 --> 19:58.551
Sell 'em to a scrapyard
for some extra dough?

20:00.720 --> 20:02.347
Eh, you got a dollar
in your wallet, kid.

20:02.347 --> 20:04.140
Can you afford
to think that small?

20:05.767 --> 20:07.060
No goddamn ambition.

20:09.104 --> 20:11.189
Snuff out the fire.
We're losing time.

20:14.526 --> 20:15.819
[menacing music playing]

20:28.707 --> 20:29.708
All right, good here.

20:34.546 --> 20:38.800
[metal clanking]

20:39.801 --> 20:41.428
[pants]

20:43.805 --> 20:44.806
On three.

20:46.099 --> 20:47.016
[grunts]

20:47.016 --> 20:49.310
Uh, you know what? Just do it.

20:50.061 --> 20:51.312
[both grunting]

20:54.441 --> 20:56.109
[body bag unzipping]

21:00.447 --> 21:01.614
[Oz sighs]

21:03.033 --> 21:05.118
[breathing heavily]

21:12.083 --> 21:13.126
Hold up there, chief.

21:15.170 --> 21:16.421
There's a nice sunrise
behind you.

21:16.546 --> 21:17.672
You should take a look.

21:20.425 --> 21:21.259
Go on.

21:21.551 --> 21:24.012
[sighs] Please don't do this.
No.

21:25.305 --> 21:26.347
Hey, wait.

21:26.973 --> 21:28.266
No, no, no, no.

21:28.266 --> 21:30.268
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hey!

21:30.393 --> 21:31.394
Stop!

21:33.646 --> 21:34.856
Ever had one of these?

21:41.905 --> 21:43.114
[lighter opens]

21:45.116 --> 21:47.202
[lighter clicking]

21:47.744 --> 21:49.621
[puffing]

21:49.621 --> 21:50.580
There you go.

21:51.956 --> 21:52.957
[Victor coughing]

21:57.921 --> 21:59.506
His name's Alberto Falcone.

22:00.507 --> 22:02.550
He's the new king--
Well, was the new kingpin

22:02.550 --> 22:03.885
of the Falcone mob.

22:04.636 --> 22:05.929
[Victor sighs heavily]

22:06.054 --> 22:06.930
Yeah.

22:07.472 --> 22:08.973
So, the smart play here
is to kill you

22:09.099 --> 22:10.558
and stuff you in the trunk
with Stinky,

22:10.558 --> 22:12.102
- be done with both of youse.
- No, no, no.

22:12.102 --> 22:13.478
We-we don't have to--

22:13.603 --> 22:15.563
It's a goddamn fact, Vic.
It just is.

22:15.563 --> 22:17.941
No, no, no, no, no.
Wait. Wait! Hold on!

22:18.483 --> 22:19.401
You can't.

22:20.110 --> 22:22.195
[breathing raggedly]
I could help you.

22:22.696 --> 22:23.613
You know?

22:25.031 --> 22:26.741
With whatever you need,
I can help you.

22:26.741 --> 22:28.201
Yeah. And how do I need you?

22:31.496 --> 22:32.664
I got ambition.

22:33.540 --> 22:36.334
And I'm not...
I'm not a waste, okay? I'm not.

22:36.334 --> 22:39.337
I could... I could help you
w-with whatever it is.

22:39.337 --> 22:42.549
Wh-wh-whatever you need,
whatever it is, all right?

22:43.091 --> 22:45.176
I just-- [sighs]

22:45.176 --> 22:46.845
Please, I need a chance.

22:48.304 --> 22:50.432
- I need a chance!
- All right, calm down.

22:50.932 --> 22:52.475
[train passing]

23:02.444 --> 23:03.737
[somber music playing]

23:03.737 --> 23:06.156
Well, maybe it'd be useful,
keeping you around.

23:06.156 --> 23:07.115
For now.

23:08.158 --> 23:09.492
See if you got what you say.

23:10.952 --> 23:12.495
But if you step out of line
just once,

23:12.495 --> 23:14.706
I swear to God, I'll gut you
like a fucking fish.

23:14.831 --> 23:15.665
Do you understand?

23:15.665 --> 23:17.459
[weakly] Yeah. Yeah. Yes.

23:17.459 --> 23:18.960
- Do you understand?
- Yeah. Yeah.

23:18.960 --> 23:20.128
Good.

23:23.882 --> 23:24.966
Now, shut the fuck up.

23:26.009 --> 23:27.343
I wanna watch the sunrise.

23:28.053 --> 23:29.471
[somber music playing]

23:55.080 --> 23:56.748
[door locks]

24:00.335 --> 24:01.127
[thud]

24:01.127 --> 24:02.796
We ain't got a lot of time.

24:03.838 --> 24:05.090
I gotta be at work soon.

24:05.215 --> 24:06.257
[water running]

24:06.424 --> 24:08.843
'Cause, you know,
it's any other day.

24:09.594 --> 24:10.887
- [gulps, sighs]
- [glass thuds]

24:10.887 --> 24:12.722
You can use the sink
to clean up.

24:14.557 --> 24:16.059
Touch anything, I'll know.

24:18.436 --> 24:19.479
[door closes]

24:36.287 --> 24:37.622
[brace squeaking]

24:37.622 --> 24:38.998
[brace clatters to floor]

24:41.459 --> 24:45.130
[Oz sighing]

24:46.840 --> 24:47.966
[sighs]

24:50.719 --> 24:52.053
[sighs]

24:59.269 --> 25:00.311
[metal jangling]

25:05.150 --> 25:06.359
[tense music playing]

25:16.494 --> 25:19.164
- [sirens in distance]
- [jackhammer running]

25:23.877 --> 25:25.086
[somber music playing]

25:27.088 --> 25:28.173
Look at this.

25:29.674 --> 25:31.676
What that fucking madman did.

25:43.813 --> 25:46.358
[upbeat hip-hop music playing]

25:47.317 --> 25:50.570
- [bill counter whirring]
- [indistinct chatter]

25:54.407 --> 25:55.867
Hey, Nick, come here.

25:55.992 --> 25:58.453
Bring a pen
and, uh, one of them envelopes.

25:59.496 --> 26:00.372
What's up?

26:01.539 --> 26:04.084
Get this to Councilman Hady.

26:04.834 --> 26:07.545
He's a... big fan of Bella Reál.

26:08.963 --> 26:09.839
He, uh...

26:10.507 --> 26:12.759
likes to tout himself
as one of the good ones,

26:13.385 --> 26:15.637
but he got into
some serious debt with Carmine.

26:15.637 --> 26:17.847
We all got our own vices.

26:18.473 --> 26:19.641
All right.

26:20.183 --> 26:22.143
Make sure he knows
it's from me, all right?

26:22.143 --> 26:23.353
Come on, kid.

26:29.609 --> 26:31.361
Hey, Doc. How we lookin'?

26:31.486 --> 26:34.030
Well, we've recovered
about 30% of the product.

26:34.030 --> 26:35.865
There's a risk of contamination.

26:35.865 --> 26:38.034
Most of the Drops
were fished out of sewer water.

26:38.034 --> 26:40.078
That ain't gonna stop Dropheads
from buying it.

26:40.203 --> 26:41.079
[laughs] No.

26:41.204 --> 26:42.247
Give the people
what they want.

26:42.372 --> 26:43.331
- All right.
- [banging]

26:43.456 --> 26:44.874
- [man 1] Get him in.
- [man 2 groans]

26:44.874 --> 26:46.126
[Oz] What the fuck is that?

26:47.168 --> 26:48.044
[man 2 groaning]

26:48.712 --> 26:50.046
[Oz] Mikey,
what the hell happened?

26:50.046 --> 26:51.840
Got jumped by the Odessa Mob, maybe.

26:51.840 --> 26:53.842
Or Burnley Town.
I don't know. It happened fast.

26:53.842 --> 26:55.677
But they got
the whole fucking stash.

26:55.677 --> 26:57.846
- What the fuck? Son of a bitch!
- [Mikey] Yep.

26:57.846 --> 27:00.098
Now we got every asshole
on the street testing fences.

27:00.223 --> 27:01.266
- It's fucking crazy.
- Oz!

27:01.266 --> 27:02.767
- What?
- It's the Family.

27:02.892 --> 27:04.269
- They wanna talk to you.
- Yeah.

27:04.811 --> 27:05.937
Get him outta here, to the back.

27:05.937 --> 27:07.355
You got it.
Let's get the man up.

27:07.355 --> 27:10.025
[men murmuring, grunting]

27:10.025 --> 27:11.568
- [Mikey] Let's go, buddy.
- [man groaning]

27:11.568 --> 27:12.527
[Mikey] Come on.

27:14.946 --> 27:15.780
Yeah.

27:15.780 --> 27:18.158
[foreboding music playing]

27:23.705 --> 27:26.958
So, uh, what does that, uh,
what does that mean exactly,

27:26.958 --> 27:28.460
to... to be called in?

27:29.044 --> 27:30.045
Could mean anything.

27:30.170 --> 27:32.922
Do you... do you think
that they know?

27:32.922 --> 27:34.049
Jesus, kid.

27:34.591 --> 27:36.384
Am I holding
a fucking crystal ball?

27:41.639 --> 27:43.058
It's all a song and dance.

27:43.725 --> 27:45.393
Nine times out of ten,
these top-tier guys

27:45.393 --> 27:47.145
wanna meet face-to-face
to feel big,

27:47.145 --> 27:48.938
so I make myself small,

27:48.938 --> 27:50.273
they feel better
about themselves,

27:50.273 --> 27:51.691
and I get to go back to work.

27:52.609 --> 27:54.611
[coughs] This is us.

28:06.539 --> 28:07.791
Damn!

28:19.344 --> 28:21.179
All right, listen,
if I don't come out...

28:25.433 --> 28:26.643
Nah, I'll be fine.

28:26.768 --> 28:28.812
You'll be fine.
It's-it's gonna be fine.

28:31.147 --> 28:33.316
I'm messing with you, kid.
All right, just sit tight.

28:33.316 --> 28:34.693
Maybe look
for your sense of humor.

28:34.818 --> 28:36.444
It's gotta be here somewhere.

28:51.918 --> 28:52.836
Fellas.

29:01.302 --> 29:02.637
Johnny. Milos.

29:02.637 --> 29:03.930
Have a seat.

29:07.851 --> 29:10.979
Lot of pomp and circumstance
to be coming out here like this.

29:11.438 --> 29:13.356
[laughs]
Not that I'm complaining.

29:17.318 --> 29:19.738
So, uh, we got something
to celebrate, or what?

29:20.780 --> 29:22.449
We've decided
to shut down the plant.

29:22.949 --> 29:25.243
We're gonna move all operations
to Robbinsville.

29:25.785 --> 29:27.537
Hold up. [laughs]

29:27.537 --> 29:28.913
Wh-what are you talking about?

29:28.913 --> 29:31.249
There's a lot less heat
in Robbinsville.

29:31.374 --> 29:33.209
Yeah, there's
a lot less business, too.

29:33.835 --> 29:35.879
You know how much cash
my guys bring in?

29:35.879 --> 29:38.339
This is my operation.
You can't just shut it down.

29:38.798 --> 29:39.716
No.

29:40.175 --> 29:42.635
This is our operation.
It's our guys.

29:42.635 --> 29:45.221
You work for the Family.
Have you forgotten that?

29:45.889 --> 29:47.724
[Milos] Oz, we're consolidating.

29:47.849 --> 29:49.893
Most of the supplies,
they were damaged in the flood.

29:49.893 --> 29:51.102
Actually, that ain't true.

29:51.311 --> 29:53.355
Nah, we recovered
a lot of the product, 70%.

29:53.355 --> 29:55.398
It doesn't matter, all right?
The police are circling.

29:55.398 --> 29:57.108
Got a target on our back.
Gangs encroaching.

29:57.233 --> 29:59.027
There's blood in the water.
Everyone knows it.

29:59.027 --> 30:00.612
- And you wanna bail?
- Jesus Christ!

30:00.737 --> 30:02.530
If we don't protect what's ours,
we look weak.

30:02.530 --> 30:03.573
This isn't your call.

30:03.990 --> 30:05.533
You're handing the Maronis
or someone worse

30:05.533 --> 30:07.452
the keys to the fucking kingdom.
Don't you get that?

30:07.452 --> 30:09.746
[Viti] The last thing we need
is a goddamn gang war!

30:09.746 --> 30:11.915
Now, Milos asked you here
as a courtesy,

30:12.040 --> 30:13.541
because he's a courteous guy.

30:13.541 --> 30:14.501
I am not.

30:15.043 --> 30:16.294
You will do as you're told.

30:18.963 --> 30:19.839
You're free to leave.

30:24.010 --> 30:25.845
Well, wait a second.

30:29.307 --> 30:30.809
What if I could fix it?

30:30.934 --> 30:31.810
This?

30:32.602 --> 30:35.230
I mean, at the end of the day,
this is all about money, right?

30:35.939 --> 30:38.441
Maybe we don't see eye-to-eye
on every little thing.

30:38.441 --> 30:40.026
You know,
maybe you don't like me.

30:40.610 --> 30:42.904
That's fine.
I'm an acquired taste.

30:43.571 --> 30:44.698
But I make you money.

30:45.532 --> 30:47.033
And I got wind
of a shipment coming in.

30:47.826 --> 30:50.286
I don't wanna tout it too much,
but it's big.

30:50.286 --> 30:51.579
In fact, it's got the potential

30:51.579 --> 30:53.498
to revolutionize
the drug business.

30:54.708 --> 30:57.752
- [Viti] What kind of shipment?
- I can't reveal the details yet.

30:57.752 --> 30:59.462
Nah, nah, but it's brand-new.

31:00.588 --> 31:02.841
Something that'll help us
expand beyond Drops.

31:03.508 --> 31:06.177
And all you guys gotta do is
sit back and reap the rewards.

31:06.302 --> 31:07.721
I'll oversee the whole thing.

31:07.846 --> 31:10.223
I'll use some of the crew.
I'll run it out of the plant.

31:16.896 --> 31:17.939
Was that a yes or...?

31:18.523 --> 31:20.984
Sofia, please, join us.

31:20.984 --> 31:22.569
Oh, I didn't mean to interrupt.

31:23.695 --> 31:24.988
[suspenseful music playing]

31:27.365 --> 31:29.367
Oz, you remember
Carmine's daughter?

31:29.367 --> 31:30.368
Yeah.

31:30.994 --> 31:31.953
Sofia...

31:32.412 --> 31:34.330
I thought
you were still at, uh...

31:37.042 --> 31:38.960
- Arkham?
- Yeah.

31:40.420 --> 31:41.296
No.

31:42.881 --> 31:44.591
I've been rehabilitated.

31:46.718 --> 31:48.720
Have you asked him
about my brother?

31:50.180 --> 31:52.849
- I thought we agreed--
- Have you heard from Alberto?

31:53.516 --> 31:55.310
- Sofia, please...
- Al?

31:55.310 --> 31:57.562
He went out last night,
he refused his bodyguards,

31:57.562 --> 31:58.897
and he never came home.

31:58.897 --> 31:59.898
Sofia, that's enough.

32:01.858 --> 32:03.902
I-I better get out of your hair.

32:04.694 --> 32:06.363
You know, let you...

32:07.197 --> 32:09.074
So we can talk about this again?

32:09.616 --> 32:10.658
Shut it down.

32:11.284 --> 32:12.786
You have 48 hours.

32:15.288 --> 32:16.164
I'll get it done.

32:16.706 --> 32:18.917
You know, whatever...
whatever helps the Family.

32:20.585 --> 32:22.796
And, uh, it's good to see you.

32:33.390 --> 32:34.724
Fuckin' assholes.

32:37.894 --> 32:38.812
Oz.

32:39.479 --> 32:40.355
A moment.

32:41.439 --> 32:43.024
You never gave me an answer.

32:43.983 --> 32:45.276
Have you seen Alberto?

32:45.276 --> 32:46.194
Oh, yeah. Right.

32:46.194 --> 32:47.362
Uh, no. No.

32:47.362 --> 32:50.573
He's the boss now,
so he's a busy man.

32:51.116 --> 32:52.492
But I'm sure he's fine.

32:53.702 --> 32:55.036
They said the same thing.

32:55.036 --> 32:56.371
- Milos and Johnny?
- Mm-hmm.

32:56.371 --> 32:57.330
Well, they'd know.

32:58.289 --> 32:59.290
[Sofia] Mmm.

33:00.709 --> 33:01.584
Well...

33:02.794 --> 33:03.837
Better get back to it.

33:05.046 --> 33:06.297
This is yours?

33:07.632 --> 33:09.592
This? [chuckles] Yeah.

33:11.803 --> 33:12.804
Purple.

33:14.055 --> 33:14.931
Very subtle.

33:15.265 --> 33:17.559
Well, technically, it's plum,
you know?

33:17.559 --> 33:19.477
Leather seats
come standard, too, so...

33:19.477 --> 33:20.520
[Sofia] Mmm.

33:21.604 --> 33:23.940
You've really moved up
in the world, haven't you?

33:26.234 --> 33:27.110
Oh.

33:29.904 --> 33:31.239
What happened here?

33:31.781 --> 33:32.991
Uh...

33:33.116 --> 33:36.119
Punk kids tried to steal my rims
a few days back.

33:36.119 --> 33:38.788
I missed, but they got
the message. [chuckles]

33:39.372 --> 33:41.791
We're long overdue
for a catch-up, you and me.

33:43.126 --> 33:44.419
Let's get a bite to eat.

33:47.630 --> 33:48.965
- Right now?
- Right now.

33:50.341 --> 33:51.468
I know a place.

33:52.135 --> 33:54.054
[classical music
playing quietly]

33:55.555 --> 33:57.599
[Sofia sighs, chews hungrily]

34:00.185 --> 34:05.023
[inhaling and sighing]

34:05.148 --> 34:06.608
[Oz chuckles softly]

34:10.278 --> 34:12.197
Another dirty martini.
Three olives.

34:12.197 --> 34:13.573
You ready for another one?

34:13.740 --> 34:16.201
- You can make that two actually.
- [busboy] Right away.

34:19.204 --> 34:22.332
[sighs] It's a bit stuffy
for my tastes.

34:22.332 --> 34:24.042
My father used to bring
me and Alberto here

34:24.042 --> 34:25.210
when we were kids.

34:28.046 --> 34:30.507
He paid us to keep our elbows
off the table.

34:31.007 --> 34:32.217
[Sofia chuckles]

34:32.342 --> 34:33.968
Well, who's stopping you now, huh?

34:37.639 --> 34:38.473
There you go.

34:38.473 --> 34:40.475
[both chuckle]

34:47.065 --> 34:49.150
You think they're wondering
if it's really me?

34:51.069 --> 34:52.028
Well, I would.

34:52.737 --> 34:56.241
What, is a psycho killer
just roaming around free,

34:56.241 --> 34:57.242
having a salad?

34:58.993 --> 35:00.328
What did the Gazette call me?

35:01.037 --> 35:02.205
The Hangman?

35:03.665 --> 35:05.750
The guards insisted
that I read every article,

35:05.750 --> 35:07.168
that I see all the stories.

35:08.044 --> 35:09.713
If only I'd been
a dutiful daughter.

35:15.385 --> 35:16.761
Are you nervous, Oz?

35:17.595 --> 35:18.513
Nervous?

35:20.390 --> 35:22.350
I'd hate for you
to feel nervous with me.

35:23.935 --> 35:26.271
'Cause despite what you
might think, I don't blame you.

35:26.396 --> 35:28.940
You know, if you hadn't gone
to my father...

35:30.483 --> 35:32.193
He left you no choice.

35:32.193 --> 35:35.238
Yeah, sure. But, eh,
I coulda done something--

35:35.363 --> 35:36.239
Let's not do that.

35:36.781 --> 35:37.907
Daddy is dead.

35:38.867 --> 35:40.035
And we are...

35:42.078 --> 35:43.246
untamed.

35:45.540 --> 35:46.416
[glasses clink]

35:48.168 --> 35:49.294
[Oz sips]

35:49.419 --> 35:50.295
[Oz sets down glass]

35:52.964 --> 35:55.258
Alberto told me he was going
to your club last night

35:55.258 --> 35:56.843
to get to my father's loft.

35:59.262 --> 36:00.263
[tense music playing]

36:00.263 --> 36:01.890
I insisted I go with him, but...

36:01.890 --> 36:03.391
he's been so protective of me.

36:03.391 --> 36:04.934
He didn't want me
leaving the house.

36:06.102 --> 36:09.230
It was all part of this plan
he cooked up.

36:09.230 --> 36:10.940
It was our shared secret.

36:11.566 --> 36:14.819
But then today, I hear you

36:14.819 --> 36:17.614
talking about revolutionizing
the drug business,

36:17.614 --> 36:19.199
and it just doesn't sit right.

36:20.950 --> 36:22.660
How do you know about his plan,

36:22.786 --> 36:25.997
and why on Earth
would you pitch it as your own?

36:28.792 --> 36:31.836
You know, it's so brazen

36:32.837 --> 36:36.257
that you either have to be
blindingly stupid

36:36.883 --> 36:38.134
or wildly confident

36:38.134 --> 36:40.887
that he isn't coming back
to reclaim it.

36:41.012 --> 36:43.056
So, I'm going to ask you again.

36:44.849 --> 36:46.434
Do you know where my brother is?

36:47.894 --> 36:49.187
Listen, Sofia...

36:50.397 --> 36:51.272
[chuckles]

36:53.400 --> 36:54.526
I'm an asshole.

36:56.319 --> 36:57.904
But you're the surprise here.

36:58.822 --> 36:59.948
Excuse me?

36:59.948 --> 37:01.825
Al never told me you was back...

37:02.784 --> 37:04.786
or that you were in on
this thing with us.

37:04.786 --> 37:07.205
Yeah, he's keeping us both
in the dark,

37:07.330 --> 37:08.415
and I don't know why.

37:09.499 --> 37:12.043
But you're right.
Alberto trusted me.

37:12.043 --> 37:13.169
And my stupid mouth...

37:13.169 --> 37:14.838
[inhales]
You know, I screwed up.

37:16.172 --> 37:17.757
Maybe you could put in
a good word.

37:18.383 --> 37:20.593
I mean, I-I don't wanna
put that on you, but...

37:22.011 --> 37:23.805
He was so passionate
about his plan,

37:23.805 --> 37:25.932
I thought there's no reason
not to move forward,

37:26.057 --> 37:28.059
just 'cause he's
on another bender, you know?

37:28.059 --> 37:31.021
I mean, the shipment arrives
in a few days, right?

37:32.605 --> 37:33.857
What do you mean "a bender"?

37:37.902 --> 37:39.571
Al's an addict, sweetheart.

37:40.655 --> 37:42.157
He's got a penchant for Drops.

37:42.949 --> 37:44.534
And booze and gambling.

37:44.534 --> 37:46.202
I'm pretty sure
he's got a sex thing, too.

37:46.202 --> 37:48.580
So yeah, this ain't
the first time he's gone AWOL.

37:48.705 --> 37:50.123
But he always comes back.

37:50.999 --> 37:54.794
Look, if he was at my club,
I wouldn't know.

37:56.046 --> 37:57.380
I was actually
drowning my sorrows

37:57.380 --> 37:59.507
with my lady friend
last night, Eve.

38:02.260 --> 38:04.596
If it'll make you feel better,
let's you and me go there now.

38:04.596 --> 38:06.056
We'll scour the joint.

38:06.056 --> 38:08.516
I doubt anything will turn up,
but it's worth a shot.

38:09.059 --> 38:10.894
You know, whatever puts
your mind at ease.

38:15.940 --> 38:16.941
No, Oz, you're right.

38:19.277 --> 38:20.820
I'm probably just being crazy.

38:27.786 --> 38:29.329
Let's stay and enjoy the meal.

38:31.915 --> 38:33.917
- I know I could use a good one.
- [Oz chuckles]

38:33.917 --> 38:35.293
He'll turn up, Sofia.

38:36.628 --> 38:37.462
I'm sure of it.

38:38.922 --> 38:39.964
[glasses clink]

38:40.256 --> 38:42.217
[Oz] Thanks for lunch.
I'll get the next one.

38:45.553 --> 38:46.596
[kisses]

38:46.596 --> 38:47.972
You know, Oz,

38:47.972 --> 38:49.849
people underestimate you,
but not me.

38:50.934 --> 38:53.061
I've always known
you were capable of more.

38:58.733 --> 39:01.695
[tense music playing]

39:08.326 --> 39:10.495
[indistinct chatter]

39:12.997 --> 39:14.124
Where are we going?

39:17.252 --> 39:18.586
[train trundling]

39:18.586 --> 39:20.922
[indistinct announcement
over PA]

39:22.006 --> 39:25.468
Are-are we in trouble?

39:31.015 --> 39:33.059
[indistinct announcement
over PA]

39:39.983 --> 39:42.360
[man in mask] Scan the code.
See Gotham's true face.

39:43.028 --> 39:45.155
- Scan the code?
- Get the fuck outta here.

39:47.157 --> 39:48.450
[announcer over PA]
Irving Grove.

39:48.450 --> 39:50.035
Irving Grove Station.

39:51.703 --> 39:53.288
Irving Grove Station.

39:57.792 --> 39:58.877
This is yours?

40:00.128 --> 40:01.004
Get in.

40:09.721 --> 40:11.014
[engine turning]

40:11.014 --> 40:12.932
[through speakers]
♪ Working 9 to 5 ♪

40:13.058 --> 40:14.476
♪ What a way to make a-- ♪

40:14.476 --> 40:15.810
[song ends abruptly]

40:18.646 --> 40:19.731
[car shifts into gear]

40:21.733 --> 40:25.737
[train passing]

40:25.862 --> 40:28.656
[children laughing,
chattering indistinctly]

40:28.656 --> 40:29.824
[brakes squeaking]

40:32.702 --> 40:33.661
[engine turns off]

40:42.128 --> 40:44.089
[Oz] I ain't never taken
anyone here before.

40:44.714 --> 40:45.924
You say a word to anybody...

40:46.049 --> 40:47.092
You'll gut me like a fish.

40:47.092 --> 40:48.718
Yeah, till you bleed out
and die.

40:51.805 --> 40:54.099
Oh, and mind
your friggin' manners, too.

41:01.022 --> 41:01.898
Here.

41:03.441 --> 41:04.317
Don't move.

41:06.569 --> 41:07.779
[woman] What're you doing here?

41:07.904 --> 41:09.364
[Oz] What do you mean
what am I doing here?

41:09.364 --> 41:10.448
I came to see you.

41:10.448 --> 41:11.950
Huh? Princess.

41:12.534 --> 41:13.743
[Oz chuckles]

41:13.910 --> 41:16.579
- [woman] You look handsome. Oh!
- [Oz] Thank you.

41:16.579 --> 41:18.915
- [woman] Put it on straight.
- [Oz] Close your eyes.

41:18.915 --> 41:21.126
- I got you something. Come here.
- [woman] What did you do?

41:21.251 --> 41:22.460
[Oz] I'll tell you when.

41:23.461 --> 41:25.964
[woman] Wha... Wait.
[laughing] What did you do?

41:26.089 --> 41:28.466
[Oz] Okay, now look,
keep 'em closed.

41:28.466 --> 41:29.968
[woman] They're closed.
They're closed.

41:29.968 --> 41:33.096
All right. Open your eyes.

41:33.096 --> 41:35.473
[gasps, laughs softly]

41:36.349 --> 41:38.727
Oswald, it's too much.

41:38.727 --> 41:41.271
- [gasps] No.
- It's perfect.

41:41.271 --> 41:42.313
It suits ya, Ma.

41:42.814 --> 41:44.065
Uh...

41:44.607 --> 41:46.234
- Thank you, sweetheart.
- You're welcome.

41:46.234 --> 41:48.069
[Francis] That's crazy.

41:48.069 --> 41:50.405
Wait, wait, wait.
Was I expecting you?

41:50.405 --> 41:51.990
- It's not Sunday, is it?
- [Oz] No, it's--

41:52.115 --> 41:54.284
- [Francis] I didn't get--
- [Oz] Nah, nah.

41:54.284 --> 41:55.785
No, it's a special occasion.

41:55.785 --> 41:57.996
We're gonna... We're gonna
leave town for a while.

41:57.996 --> 42:00.498
- Ah.
- [Oz] Take a little vacation.

42:00.498 --> 42:03.001
A vacation? To where?
You know I hate flying.

42:03.001 --> 42:04.335
Yeah. We're gonna drive.

42:04.961 --> 42:07.172
We're gonna drive?
Who-who's gonna drive?

42:07.172 --> 42:08.423
You gonna drive?

42:09.049 --> 42:10.508
- [Oz] Ma?
- [Francis] What?

42:10.508 --> 42:12.635
Why is this in the tub?
Your pills are ruined.

42:12.635 --> 42:14.304
No. I take 'em every morning
with breakfast.

42:14.304 --> 42:15.805
The tub is full.

42:15.805 --> 42:17.182
The boys were playing
in the bath.

42:17.307 --> 42:18.391
They didn't wanna get out.

42:22.937 --> 42:23.772
What?

42:23.772 --> 42:24.814
Oh, nothing.

42:25.565 --> 42:27.776
How about let's take your meds
right now, huh?

42:29.527 --> 42:30.528
Just to be sure.

42:30.528 --> 42:32.489
[mutters mockingly]

42:33.156 --> 42:34.324
I took 'em.

42:34.324 --> 42:35.867
The pills are by the sink.

42:35.867 --> 42:37.243
[screaming] Oswald!

42:37.786 --> 42:38.870
- Someone's here.
- Ooh. Um...

42:38.995 --> 42:40.372
- Get out of my house!
- Hi. I'm...

42:40.497 --> 42:43.208
Who the hell is this?
Who the hell are you? What?

42:43.208 --> 42:45.335
- Shit! Ma, sorry. This is Vic.
- Get out!

42:45.335 --> 42:46.920
He's gonna help
take care of you.

42:47.379 --> 42:48.880
Just in case I need
to handle some things

42:48.880 --> 42:50.048
while we're gone. All right?

42:50.173 --> 42:52.425
- [Francis] Huh. Vic?
- [Oz] Yeah.

42:52.926 --> 42:55.220
- What is he, a nurse?
- Kinda.

42:55.220 --> 42:57.680
- No, I'm not--
- He's got nurse-like qualities.

42:57.680 --> 43:00.600
I'll-I'll explain more
in the car. All right? [sighs]

43:03.520 --> 43:06.106
[water running]

43:07.273 --> 43:09.109
- [Oz] All right.
- [Francis grumbles]

43:09.901 --> 43:10.985
Ma, here's your water.

43:11.194 --> 43:13.863
Take these two pills,
then we gotta go, okay?

43:14.948 --> 43:16.574
There you go, okay?

43:17.283 --> 43:20.036
Will you tell me first
what I did to lose your respect?

43:21.955 --> 43:23.748
- What are you talking about?
- You come in here,

43:23.748 --> 43:25.709
you're trying to buy me off
with a necklace?

43:26.167 --> 43:28.837
Some bullshit about
an urgent special occasion...

43:28.837 --> 43:29.796
[Oz] Ma.

43:30.046 --> 43:31.715
Did I raise my sons
to lie to me?

43:31.715 --> 43:33.425
- Did I?
- No.

43:33.425 --> 43:35.885
So, then what did you do?
What did you do?

43:35.885 --> 43:37.554
Come on. What did you do?

43:39.973 --> 43:41.015
I, uh...

43:42.475 --> 43:43.643
What did you do?

43:45.562 --> 43:46.563
I shot...

43:48.064 --> 43:49.691
Alberto Falcone.

43:51.109 --> 43:52.027
He's dead.

43:52.902 --> 43:55.321
It ain't safe for you here.
You understand?

43:55.905 --> 43:58.491
Sofia Falcone's out of Arkham,
and she knows.

43:59.200 --> 44:01.286
Uh, or if she don't, she will.

44:01.411 --> 44:02.912
Why'd you shoot him? Why?

44:02.912 --> 44:05.165
Jesus, Ma, I ain't doing this
with you right now, okay?

44:09.335 --> 44:10.462
Fine.

44:12.630 --> 44:14.883
He fuckin' laughed at me.

44:15.925 --> 44:16.801
All right?

44:18.595 --> 44:20.597
- Now, can we go please?
- He laughed at you?

44:20.722 --> 44:23.141
It was impulsive. It was stupid.
Is that what you wanna hear?

44:23.141 --> 44:24.976
Jesus, I'm trying
to take care of you.

44:24.976 --> 44:26.269
- Stop.
- I can't risk it.

44:26.269 --> 44:27.687
I can't risk you.
I'm all you got.

44:27.687 --> 44:30.023
- If something happened to me--
- Stop! Stop talking!

44:31.691 --> 44:33.485
Do you hear the words
coming out of your mouth?

44:33.610 --> 44:35.111
- Yeah.
- How weak they sound?

44:36.696 --> 44:38.031
Like a little pussy boy?

44:39.949 --> 44:40.825
Look at me.

44:41.493 --> 44:42.952
Is that what you are, Oswald?

44:43.912 --> 44:45.497
Weak little pussy boy?

44:45.622 --> 44:46.498
No.

44:48.625 --> 44:49.501
That's right.

44:50.919 --> 44:52.253
'Cause you're mine.

44:52.712 --> 44:54.798
You're my big, strong bull
of a boy.

44:54.798 --> 44:56.341
You never forget that.

44:59.052 --> 45:00.178
Come here.

45:07.352 --> 45:09.396
- [tender music playing]
- Don't you see, dear?

45:09.896 --> 45:11.731
What you did wasn't impulsive.

45:12.357 --> 45:13.608
It was instinctual.

45:14.693 --> 45:17.112
You shot that junkie piss-ant

45:17.112 --> 45:18.905
because you wanted to.

45:20.615 --> 45:21.658
Just like that.

45:23.827 --> 45:25.495
Oh, you're so close now

45:25.495 --> 45:26.871
to having everything
you ever wanted,

45:26.996 --> 45:27.872
everything you deserve.

45:27.997 --> 45:30.166
You wanna run? You wanna hide?

45:30.166 --> 45:32.085
No.

45:32.627 --> 45:34.796
This city is meant
to be yours, sweetheart.

45:38.341 --> 45:39.843
What are you gonna do to get it?

45:45.140 --> 45:46.725
[lighter clicking]

45:50.895 --> 45:52.814
["Put the Blame on Mame" playing
on television]

45:52.814 --> 45:54.524
[lighter closes, opens]

45:54.524 --> 45:55.483
[lighter clicks]

45:57.485 --> 45:58.403
[lighter closes]

46:00.864 --> 46:05.243
♪ They once had a shootin'
up in the Klondike ♪

46:05.243 --> 46:08.246
♪ When they got Dan McGrew ♪

46:08.246 --> 46:09.372
[volume increases]

46:09.706 --> 46:13.376
♪ Folks were putting
the blame on ♪

46:13.376 --> 46:14.377
[Oz sighs]

46:14.544 --> 46:17.464
♪ The lady known as Lou ♪

46:18.715 --> 46:21.051
♪ That's the story
that went around ♪

46:21.051 --> 46:22.469
God damn it, this chick.

46:22.469 --> 46:25.305
♪ But here's the real lowdown ♪

46:27.098 --> 46:30.226
♪ Put the blame on Mame, boys ♪

46:30.226 --> 46:32.103
[chuckles] Who's Mame?

46:32.228 --> 46:34.189
♪ Put the blame on Mame ♪

46:34.189 --> 46:35.315
It don't matter, kid.

46:36.483 --> 46:37.609
That's the thing.

46:38.943 --> 46:40.320
She's just a scapegoat.

46:40.445 --> 46:43.656
♪ That's the thing
that slew McGrew ♪

46:44.574 --> 46:48.286
♪ Put the blame on Mame, boys ♪

46:48.286 --> 46:51.831
♪ Put the blame ♪

46:51.831 --> 46:56.920
♪ On Mame ♪

46:57.045 --> 46:57.921
[song ends]

46:57.921 --> 46:59.172
[train horn sounds]

47:00.840 --> 47:03.176
[Oz] Listen, it ain't easy,
but your part in this...

47:03.718 --> 47:04.928
it's the most important.

47:05.512 --> 47:07.180
So don't say you're good
unless you are.

47:09.474 --> 47:11.518
I don't know, Oz.
I don't know if I'm, uh...

47:13.603 --> 47:16.815
I've-I've n-never done
anything like this.

47:16.815 --> 47:17.941
Oh.

47:21.945 --> 47:23.196
Listen, Vic, uh...

47:24.280 --> 47:25.573
the tenement where you live...

47:27.033 --> 47:28.243
I know it's gone.

47:28.868 --> 47:30.620
Nothing on Sixth
was left standing.

47:30.620 --> 47:34.249
I don't know if you had family
or people in there...

47:36.251 --> 47:37.252
but you made it.

47:37.877 --> 47:39.212
You're standing right here.

47:40.296 --> 47:41.423
I've been where you are.

47:41.881 --> 47:43.174
And you heard my ma.

47:43.299 --> 47:44.801
I mean, this...

47:44.801 --> 47:47.470
this is one of those moments
where you gotta ask yourself...

47:48.054 --> 47:49.264
what kind of life do I want?

47:50.098 --> 47:52.475
You wanna spend your days
thinking small, stealing rims,

47:52.475 --> 47:53.768
barely getting by?

47:54.728 --> 47:56.229
Or do you want more
for yourself?

47:57.772 --> 47:59.441
You saw how the Falcones live.

48:00.150 --> 48:02.610
Can you imagine
living like that? Huh?

48:02.610 --> 48:06.197
In a mansion,
maids and butlers and shit?

48:06.322 --> 48:07.615
They don't even know
what they got,

48:07.615 --> 48:08.867
'cause they always had it.

48:10.201 --> 48:11.202
Never hungry.

48:11.953 --> 48:12.912
Born full.

48:14.581 --> 48:15.498
Not us.

48:18.168 --> 48:20.545
The world wasn't built
for guys like us.

48:21.671 --> 48:24.215
That's why we gotta take
whatever we decide is ours.

48:25.216 --> 48:27.969
'Cause no one's gonna give it
to us, not without a fight.

48:30.346 --> 48:31.639
Now, I coulda killed you.

48:32.182 --> 48:33.933
I coulda put you
out of your misery,

48:33.933 --> 48:34.976
but I didn't,

48:35.185 --> 48:36.770
'cause you need
a guy like me, Vic.

48:37.896 --> 48:38.938
But I gotta know.

48:40.815 --> 48:41.733
No bullshit.

48:43.943 --> 48:45.570
Can I count on you
to pull through?

48:48.740 --> 48:49.574
Yeah, I...

48:50.200 --> 48:51.201
I can do it.

48:51.743 --> 48:52.744
Huh?

48:53.453 --> 48:54.621
I can do it.

48:54.746 --> 48:56.456
[suspenseful music playing]

48:57.916 --> 48:59.084
I know you can.

49:00.627 --> 49:03.129
What do you think? I hire
any schmuck off the street? No.

49:04.089 --> 49:06.049
- [Oz chuckles]
- [Victor chuckles softly]

49:06.883 --> 49:09.052
All right, go ahead.
Get outta here.

49:09.636 --> 49:10.512
Keep your phone on.

49:11.012 --> 49:12.931
[suspenseful music continues]

49:21.731 --> 49:23.900
[inmates shouting indistinctly]

49:29.114 --> 49:30.657
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door unlocks]

49:35.537 --> 49:36.413
[door clangs shut]

49:37.288 --> 49:38.915
[inmates shouting in distance]

49:40.291 --> 49:41.751
[buzzer sounds]

49:41.751 --> 49:43.044
[door unlocks]

49:48.133 --> 49:49.008
Sal.

49:50.135 --> 49:51.469
That's not my table.

49:57.517 --> 49:59.519
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door unlocks]

50:05.650 --> 50:07.694
Listen, Sal, I'm here
to make things right.

50:08.820 --> 50:10.488
I'm done with the Falcones.

50:10.488 --> 50:13.158
I wanna offer my services
to you and your family.

50:13.158 --> 50:15.827
Well, that surprises me, Oz.
Really does.

50:16.536 --> 50:19.372
'Cause I thought you liked
eating outta Falcone's ass.

50:20.123 --> 50:21.916
Oh, you wanna throw stones?

50:21.916 --> 50:22.834
[chuckles]

50:22.834 --> 50:23.793
Fine.

50:24.753 --> 50:25.920
But from where I sit,

50:26.463 --> 50:27.714
and where you sit,

50:28.465 --> 50:29.883
I don't think
you're in a position

50:29.883 --> 50:31.009
not to hear me out.

50:31.634 --> 50:33.094
Way I see it,

50:33.094 --> 50:35.305
the Falcone higher-ups are
a bunch of old men who don't...

50:35.305 --> 50:36.431
No disrespect.

50:36.431 --> 50:37.766
...who don't remember
what it's like

50:37.766 --> 50:39.017
to get their hands dirty.

50:39.017 --> 50:41.186
That's what they hire
guys like me for,

50:41.311 --> 50:43.563
which means I got direct access
to the ground game.

50:44.064 --> 50:46.858
I'm talking the Drops,
the dealers, the chemists,

50:46.983 --> 50:48.026
the whole thing.

50:48.985 --> 50:49.986
Next couple of days,

50:50.362 --> 50:52.697
the Falcones are gonna do
something real stupid.

50:52.822 --> 50:55.283
They're gonna shut down
their biggest Drops operation--

50:55.283 --> 50:56.493
millions of dollars' worth--

50:56.493 --> 50:58.495
and move to some bumfuck part
of Gotham,

50:59.079 --> 51:00.538
which means a huge chunk
of their business

51:00.538 --> 51:01.915
will be ripe for the taking.

51:03.249 --> 51:04.959
And guess
who's in charge of the move.

51:05.794 --> 51:07.379
I could give you
everything you need.

51:07.504 --> 51:10.799
So your crew could just swoop in
and steal the whole fucking kit.

51:10.799 --> 51:11.966
I play victim.

51:12.759 --> 51:14.177
We split the payday.

51:14.761 --> 51:16.304
You make it sound so simple.

51:17.430 --> 51:19.724
But it's my guys
doing all the heavy lifting.

51:19.849 --> 51:21.851
Yeah, revenge don't come easy.

51:23.019 --> 51:24.354
Come on, Sal.

51:25.563 --> 51:27.399
Don't you fucking miss it?

51:29.609 --> 51:30.485
Respect?

51:32.070 --> 51:34.406
That's really what Carmine stole
from you, ain't it?

51:36.116 --> 51:37.534
He was a dirty rat.

51:38.493 --> 51:40.078
He played us both for fools.

51:40.870 --> 51:42.247
Ain't no changing that.

51:44.374 --> 51:45.375
But he's dead,

51:46.209 --> 51:47.502
and I'm here now,

51:47.627 --> 51:49.504
and I'm offering you
the opportunity of a lifetime.

51:49.504 --> 51:52.048
And this first hit,
it's just the beginning.

51:52.632 --> 51:54.509
I know a lot more
than people think.

51:55.427 --> 51:57.095
I'll keep playing double agent.

51:58.179 --> 51:59.055
You and me,

52:00.473 --> 52:02.058
we can tear down
their fucking empire

52:02.058 --> 52:03.143
from the inside out.

52:07.480 --> 52:09.858
What is it
you're really after, Oz?

52:09.858 --> 52:12.027
I just told you what I'm after.
What do you mean?

52:12.027 --> 52:14.779
I know who you are.
I know what you are.

52:15.363 --> 52:18.283
I don't work with people
whose loyalty is for sale.

52:18.825 --> 52:21.619
You think I forgot all the times
you schmoozed me and my boys

52:21.745 --> 52:23.246
just to turn around and fuck us?

52:23.246 --> 52:24.539
Thought I forgot that?

52:25.915 --> 52:28.543
Huge drug bust does down
right under your nose,

52:28.543 --> 52:30.211
and you got nothing
to do with it?

52:31.379 --> 52:32.505
The fuck outta here.

52:35.800 --> 52:37.927
Look, I can see you're upset.

52:38.511 --> 52:39.804
Trust takes time.

52:40.764 --> 52:42.057
But this ain't bullshit.

52:43.141 --> 52:45.643
Whoever controls Drops
controls the streets.

52:45.643 --> 52:46.936
You know that's right.

52:49.105 --> 52:50.023
So how about this?

52:50.815 --> 52:52.108
I'll come back
in a couple of days...

52:52.108 --> 52:54.486
I never wanna see
your smug face again.

52:54.611 --> 52:56.446
...we'll see
if we can't work something out.

52:57.697 --> 52:59.115
It's good seeing you.
You look good.

52:59.949 --> 53:01.409
- Fuck off.
- Think on it, Sal.

53:02.243 --> 53:03.119
Oh.

53:05.163 --> 53:06.206
I almost forgot.

53:11.628 --> 53:12.796
Ain't this yours?

53:17.425 --> 53:18.760
Where did you get this?

53:18.760 --> 53:20.470
Carmine. Wore it as his own.

53:20.470 --> 53:21.721
- [door opens]
- [laughs]

53:22.847 --> 53:23.890
The Falcones...

53:25.475 --> 53:27.394
they been flaunting
what they done to you for years.

53:27.394 --> 53:29.521
But how is it that you have it?

53:31.981 --> 53:33.608
Maybe I'm more
than what you think.

53:35.568 --> 53:36.861
[tense music playing]

53:38.279 --> 53:40.532
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door unlocks]

53:40.532 --> 53:42.409
- [engine roaring]
- [tense music playing]

53:43.785 --> 53:46.037
[on voicemail] What up?
It's Victor. Leave a message.

53:46.162 --> 53:47.080
Fuck!

54:01.177 --> 54:02.804
[bodyguards speaking
indistinctly]

54:02.804 --> 54:04.013
Nobody home.

54:08.476 --> 54:09.436
Shit!

54:12.689 --> 54:14.607
- [tires screech]
- [Sofia] Go.

54:16.860 --> 54:18.528
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

54:18.528 --> 54:20.363
- [engine roaring]
- [tires screeching]

54:20.363 --> 54:23.241
- [tense music continues]
- [breathing heavily]

54:23.366 --> 54:25.201
[tires screeching]

54:32.792 --> 54:35.045
Come on, Vic. Shit, shit, shit.

54:35.170 --> 54:36.588
[on voicemail] What up?
It's Victor.

54:36.588 --> 54:37.714
- Shit!
- Leave a message.

54:38.256 --> 54:39.591
Damn it, Vic!

54:46.514 --> 54:49.017
[tires screeching]

54:52.562 --> 54:55.482
[breathing heavily]

54:56.024 --> 54:56.900
Fuck!

54:59.527 --> 55:00.779
[indistinct chatter]

55:01.905 --> 55:03.406
[tires screeching]

55:06.242 --> 55:07.118
Let's go.

55:13.041 --> 55:14.751
Go. Go, go. Let's go.

55:17.045 --> 55:19.714
[indistinct chatter]

55:36.106 --> 55:38.024
- [gun cocks]
- Get the fuck out!

55:39.442 --> 55:41.152
["The Promise"
playing through speakers]

55:41.152 --> 55:42.237
[grunting]

55:42.779 --> 55:44.656
[Oz grunts] Come here!

55:44.781 --> 55:45.949
I'll fucking...

55:45.949 --> 55:47.992
[both grunting]

55:47.992 --> 55:49.077
[screams]

55:49.077 --> 55:50.662
♪ I'll make you fall for me ♪

55:50.662 --> 55:52.664
[both straining]

55:52.789 --> 55:54.749
♪ I promise you ♪

55:54.749 --> 55:55.709
[blade clicks]

55:56.042 --> 55:57.752
- [stabbing]
- [bodyguard screams in pain]

55:58.795 --> 56:00.922
- [grunts]
- [screams in pain]

56:02.549 --> 56:04.342
♪ And so is your temper ♪

56:04.342 --> 56:06.678
[tires screech]

56:06.678 --> 56:08.430
♪ You know what to do ♪

56:10.515 --> 56:13.184
♪ I'm gonna always be there ♪

56:13.309 --> 56:14.185
Fuck.

56:15.145 --> 56:16.146
[blows landing]

56:16.354 --> 56:19.941
[Sofia] It's a terrible feeling.
Isn't it?

56:21.067 --> 56:21.943
[blow lands]

56:22.193 --> 56:23.611
[Sofia] Nothing left
to hide behind.

56:24.446 --> 56:27.365
The guard at Arkham
stripped us bare every morning.

56:28.533 --> 56:29.784
[gasping]

56:29.784 --> 56:31.244
It was humiliating...

56:32.537 --> 56:34.039
being turned into a thing.

56:34.706 --> 56:36.458
[Oz grunts, gasps]

56:36.458 --> 56:38.835
But after a while, I just
started to think, "Well..."

56:38.835 --> 56:40.712
[breathes heavily]
"...what's it matter?

56:41.504 --> 56:42.714
There's nothing left anyway."

56:43.381 --> 56:45.633
- [Oz breathing heavily]
- But my brother?

56:45.633 --> 56:47.886
My brother
visited me every week.

56:49.095 --> 56:50.096
And every week,

56:50.263 --> 56:52.474
he said
that there was something left

56:53.224 --> 56:57.395
and that he was gonna
help me fight to keep it.

56:57.520 --> 56:58.688
[Oz gagging]

56:58.688 --> 57:01.232
[Sofia] I-I just wonder
how you see me, Oz.

57:01.358 --> 57:03.068
[gagging]

57:03.193 --> 57:08.031
If I am more
than a thing to play with.

57:08.656 --> 57:10.158
[Oz breathing heavily]

57:10.700 --> 57:12.035
[panting]

57:12.035 --> 57:16.164
You were right, though,
about the club and the loft.

57:16.831 --> 57:17.749
That was all clean.

57:18.291 --> 57:19.834
- Huh.
- [Sofia] But outside...

57:21.127 --> 57:22.879
- Well...
- [breathing shakily]

57:22.879 --> 57:26.633
The downside
of driving a plum car

57:27.425 --> 57:29.427
is that it's very hard
to forget.

57:30.804 --> 57:32.055
And so are you

57:32.222 --> 57:35.225
when you shoot at a bunch
of kids in the street.

57:35.225 --> 57:36.476
And this one...

57:37.102 --> 57:38.728
says it all happened...

57:40.647 --> 57:43.274
the night Alberto went missing.

57:46.194 --> 57:47.112
I don't know.

57:48.863 --> 57:49.864
What do you say?

57:52.575 --> 57:53.910
You think I know this kid?

57:54.703 --> 57:55.829
I don't know this kid.

57:57.163 --> 57:59.082
You can't take
some teenager's word over mine.

57:59.082 --> 58:00.917
So you're saying
that he's the liar?

58:01.793 --> 58:03.628
- Yes!
- Not you?

58:03.628 --> 58:05.463
Yes! Fucking yes!

58:05.463 --> 58:06.798
- Okay.
- [cocks gun]

58:07.340 --> 58:08.717
- Hey, no. I--
- [gun fires]

58:09.592 --> 58:11.511
[breathing heavily]

58:14.305 --> 58:17.100
[Sofia] That's what you wanted, right?

58:17.642 --> 58:20.353
To have my reputation
precede me?

58:20.895 --> 58:22.272
You are so good

58:22.272 --> 58:24.274
at talking your way
out of things.

58:24.274 --> 58:28.111
Even at the cost
of someone else's life.

58:28.903 --> 58:30.155
Especially then.

58:30.697 --> 58:31.656
Right?

58:32.282 --> 58:33.241
[line unfurling]

58:33.658 --> 58:35.160
The fuck you doing?
What are you doing?!

58:35.285 --> 58:37.162
But my father
isn't around anymore

58:37.871 --> 58:39.122
to reward you

58:39.873 --> 58:43.001
with fancy suits,
and stupid cars...

58:43.126 --> 58:44.085
Sofia.

58:44.502 --> 58:47.172
...and a club that he lets
you believe is yours.

58:48.673 --> 58:50.383
Sofia-- [screams in pain]

58:51.843 --> 58:52.969
[wailing in pain]

58:52.969 --> 58:55.055
It's just you and me now, okay?

58:55.889 --> 58:59.142
So I want you to think.
I want you to really think.

59:01.811 --> 59:02.854
Am I crazy?

59:05.440 --> 59:06.524
Is it all in my head?

59:07.067 --> 59:09.861
- [flesh tearing]
- [screaming in pain]

59:09.986 --> 59:11.446
Tell me. Tell me.

59:12.197 --> 59:14.532
Tell me that I'm...
that I'm too emotional,

59:14.657 --> 59:17.619
and that I have
an overactive imagination,

59:17.619 --> 59:24.542
and that I shouldn't take things
so personally.

59:24.542 --> 59:25.919
[menacing music playing]

59:29.214 --> 59:30.256
But first...

59:33.385 --> 59:34.677
tell me he's alive.

59:36.346 --> 59:38.848
[vehicle approaching rapidly]

59:38.848 --> 59:40.058
[crashing]

59:40.058 --> 59:42.644
[car horn blaring
uninterruptedly]

59:42.644 --> 59:44.646
[panting]

59:45.897 --> 59:47.649
[horn continues blaring]

01:00:02.080 --> 01:00:03.456
Miss Falcone, please.

01:00:06.668 --> 01:00:08.086
What the fuck is this?

01:00:12.590 --> 01:00:13.925
[tense, eerie music plays]

01:00:29.399 --> 01:00:30.483
[music intensifies]

01:00:39.200 --> 01:00:40.410
[music crescendos, fades]

01:00:40.410 --> 01:00:41.619
[gasps softly]

01:00:43.580 --> 01:00:45.081
[piercing, somber music playing]

01:00:46.875 --> 01:00:48.626
[gasps softly]

01:00:50.253 --> 01:00:51.254
[music intensifies]

01:00:54.841 --> 01:00:55.759
Oh, shit!

01:01:00.346 --> 01:01:01.431
[music turns menacing]

01:01:07.937 --> 01:01:09.814
[screaming in agony]

01:01:09.939 --> 01:01:11.733
- [Sofia's screams echo]
- [chuckles softly]

01:01:11.733 --> 01:01:14.110
[tense music playing]

01:01:14.110 --> 01:01:19.324
[laughing]

01:01:19.324 --> 01:01:21.201
[train passing]

01:01:37.467 --> 01:01:38.676
You did good today, kid.

01:01:42.180 --> 01:01:43.056
Thanks.

01:01:43.640 --> 01:01:44.808
So, I gotta ask.

01:01:46.017 --> 01:01:46.893
What happened?

01:01:48.311 --> 01:01:50.230
I mean, we made a plan.
You were there.

01:01:51.231 --> 01:01:52.357
Didn't we agree

01:01:52.357 --> 01:01:54.275
the head alone
would be the most poetic,

01:01:54.275 --> 01:01:55.985
and the pinky,
the cherry on top?

01:01:56.528 --> 01:01:58.279
But instead,
the whole body's in there.

01:01:58.279 --> 01:01:59.447
Just a pinky chopped off.

01:01:59.447 --> 01:02:00.990
It felt...

01:02:02.117 --> 01:02:03.493
well, small.

01:02:03.493 --> 01:02:07.706
Yeah, right. No, I--
Look, I-I-I wanted to, right?

01:02:07.831 --> 01:02:10.375
And I th-thought that I could,
but... [inhales deeply]

01:02:10.375 --> 01:02:12.043
When I got to it,
and I'm thinking,

01:02:12.669 --> 01:02:16.005
"Do I... Do I start at the front
and then hit the trachea?"

01:02:16.005 --> 01:02:17.382
But then
when I got to his throat,

01:02:17.382 --> 01:02:19.134
I started thinking,
"Do I cut from the back?"

01:02:19.134 --> 01:02:20.969
And then I'm imagining
the spine and...

01:02:20.969 --> 01:02:22.387
All right, all right, all right.

01:02:22.387 --> 01:02:23.680
You know what? It's fine.

01:02:24.264 --> 01:02:25.348
Room to grow.

01:02:25.849 --> 01:02:27.517
Yeah. At least Sofia
got the message.

01:02:28.017 --> 01:02:29.894
With Sal wearing that ring
around Blackgate,

01:02:30.020 --> 01:02:32.022
Maronis ain't got no choice
but to take credit.

01:02:32.522 --> 01:02:33.732
That's what matters.

01:02:34.357 --> 01:02:36.234
Wait. S-Sal doesn't know?

01:02:37.235 --> 01:02:38.945
I thought that
the whole th-thing we--

01:02:39.070 --> 01:02:40.405
Jesus, Vic, relax.

01:02:41.489 --> 01:02:43.033
We just put the Maronis
back on the map.

01:02:43.033 --> 01:02:46.077
If Sal's got a problem
with that, then... fuck him.

01:02:46.202 --> 01:02:47.412
I don't need him.

01:02:47.871 --> 01:02:48.997
I don't need any of 'em.

01:02:50.457 --> 01:02:53.376
From here on out,
there's no more playing it safe.

01:02:54.753 --> 01:02:56.296
Drops are yesterday's game.

01:02:57.672 --> 01:02:59.799
I'm gonna get whatever the hell
is in that shipment.

01:03:00.925 --> 01:03:02.594
I'm gonna run this goddamn city.

01:03:04.763 --> 01:03:05.889
And I want you in on it.

01:03:08.141 --> 01:03:08.933
Really?

01:03:09.059 --> 01:03:10.977
Yeah. You earned it.

01:03:11.811 --> 01:03:13.938
You know, for the most part.

01:03:14.522 --> 01:03:16.775
And guys like us,
we gotta stick together.

01:03:16.775 --> 01:03:18.026
[Oz slurping]

01:03:22.280 --> 01:03:24.115
It's better, right? Come on.

01:03:24.115 --> 01:03:25.408
When you mix the flavors?

01:03:26.201 --> 01:03:28.036
[laughs] Yeah, it's good.

01:03:28.036 --> 01:03:29.871
No. It's not just good.
It's better.

01:03:29.871 --> 01:03:30.914
It's the fucking best.

01:03:30.914 --> 01:03:32.457
["9 to 5"
by Dolly Parton playing]

01:03:34.084 --> 01:03:35.585
[train passing]

01:03:40.757 --> 01:03:43.134
♪ Tumble out of bed
and I stumble to the kitchen ♪

01:03:43.259 --> 01:03:45.220
♪ Pour myself
a cup of ambition ♪

01:03:45.220 --> 01:03:48.473
♪ And yawn and stretch
And try to come to life ♪

01:03:50.392 --> 01:03:52.644
♪ Jump in the shower
and the blood starts pumpin' ♪

01:03:52.769 --> 01:03:54.729
♪ Out on the street
the traffic starts jumpin' ♪

01:03:54.729 --> 01:03:58.650
♪ With folks like me
on the job from 9 to 5 ♪

01:03:59.275 --> 01:04:03.863
♪ Workin' 9 to 5
What a way to make a livin' ♪

01:04:03.863 --> 01:04:08.284
♪ Barely gettin' by
It's all takin' and no givin' ♪

01:04:08.284 --> 01:04:10.620
♪ They just use your mind ♪

01:04:10.745 --> 01:04:12.956
♪ And they never
give you credit ♪

01:04:13.081 --> 01:04:18.086
♪ It's enough to drive you
crazy if you let it ♪

01:04:18.086 --> 01:04:21.840
♪ 9 to 5
For service and devotion ♪

01:04:21.965 --> 01:04:24.342
♪ You would think that I ♪

01:04:24.467 --> 01:04:26.553
♪ Would deserve
a fair promotion ♪

01:04:26.678 --> 01:04:28.805
♪ Want to move ahead ♪

01:04:28.930 --> 01:04:31.391
♪ But the boss won't seem
to let me ♪

01:04:31.391 --> 01:04:36.187
♪ I swear sometimes
that man is out to get me ♪

01:04:36.187 --> 01:04:38.023
♪ 9 to 5, yeah ♪

01:04:38.023 --> 01:04:40.191
♪ They got you
where they want you ♪

01:04:40.191 --> 01:04:42.485
♪ There's a better life ♪

01:04:42.485 --> 01:04:44.696
♪ And you think about it,
don't you? ♪

01:04:44.696 --> 01:04:49.200
♪ It's a rich man's game
No matter what they call it ♪

01:04:49.200 --> 01:04:54.205
♪ And you spend your life
Puttin' money in his wallet ♪

01:04:54.205 --> 01:04:57.876
♪ 9 to 5
What a way to make a livin' ♪

01:04:57.876 --> 01:05:02.547
♪ Barely gettin' by
It's all takin' and no givin' ♪

01:05:02.714 --> 01:05:04.799
♪ They'll just use your mind ♪

01:05:04.799 --> 01:05:06.926
♪ And they never
give you credit ♪

01:05:07.093 --> 01:05:11.890
♪ It's enough to drive you
crazy if you let it ♪

01:05:12.223 --> 01:05:13.892
[song fades out]

01:05:15.560 --> 01:05:17.645
[dramatic music playing]

01:06:13.702 --> 01:06:14.661
[music ends]

01:06:14.828 --> 01:06:16.329
- [thunder rumbles]
- [rain pattering]

01:06:17.789 --> 01:06:18.665
[thunder rumbles]
